<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for March 11.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for March 11.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Monday announced the following forecasts and data for gas consumption for the period March 9-11.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 9 (actual) 237 mcm, 55 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 10 (forecast) 253 mcm, 59 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 11 (forecast) 257 mcm, 60 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 9 (actual) 8.5 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.9 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 10 (forecast) 7.9 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.9 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 11 (forecast) 7.4 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.0 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption across the network on Monday, and the probability of interruption on Tuesday is low.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
